# Copy this file to .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev`. .dev.vars is git-ignored.
#
# ─── App database = Cloudflare D1 (ADR 0016) — NO connection secret ─────────
# The Worker reads/writes the app database through its `DB` D1 binding, not a
# connection URL. Local `wrangler dev` uses a per-workspace local SQLite D1 that
# `pnpm dev` / `dev:preview` auto-migrate + seed via `db:setup:local`. So there is
# no app-DB secret to set locally or in deployed envs — schema is applied with
# `wrangler d1 migrations apply`. The former Prisma Accelerate `DATABASE_URL` /
# `DIRECT_URL` connection vars are fully gone (ADR 0016 / AECI-278); Supabase is
# retained for Auth only (the `SUPABASE_*` vars below).

# ─── Supabase URL + integration tests (AECI-48 / AECI-193) ──────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL is now ALSO read by the Worker at runtime (AECI-193): it drives
# JWKS user-JWT verification in `lib/user-auth.ts` (no DB round-trip). In
# deployed envs it's a wrangler `vars` entry (see wrangler.jsonc); locally,
# point it at the single SHARED AUTH project (ADR 0017 —
# https://ktuhnlypztujpsseujzx.supabase.co) so `pnpm dev:bound` verifies real
# tokens minted by the web mint script (apps/web/scripts/mint-dev-session.mjs).
#
# The integration suites (`pnpm test:integration`) read the same variable for
# PostgREST/RLS probes. For LOCAL-STACK RLS runs (supabase start), override
# per-invocation — shell-set vars beat `dotenv -e .dev.vars`:
#   SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321 \
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<local anon> SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<local secret> \
#   pnpm test:integration
# NEVER run the service-role trigger specs (auth_user_delete_trigger) against
# the shared auth project — they create/delete auth users (and that project now
# backs every environment, including production — ADR 0017). Keep
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY empty here so they self-skip; supply it only in a
# local-stack override. Tests `describe.skipIf` themselves when vars are unset.
SUPABASE_URL=
# Publishable/anon key for the project SUPABASE_URL points at.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Access token for a non-admin authenticated user. Mint a fresh one (1h
# expiry) with the kept dev tool:
#   cd apps/web && node --env-file=.dev.vars scripts/mint-dev-session.mjs
# Also consumed by the AECI-193 JWKS verification spec
# (src/integration/user-auth.jwks.spec.ts), which skips itself when unset or
# expired.
SUPABASE_TEST_USER_JWT=
# Service-role key. Used by the integration CI lane's mint step
# (.github/workflows/integration-db-tests.yml) to create a throwaway confirmed
# user via the Supabase admin API, whose freshly-issued access token feeds the
# JWKS spec. Local Supabase exposes this as the "Secret" key
# (`pnpm exec supabase status`). Never commit a real value — the Worker has no
# use for the service role at runtime and shouldn't see it.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ─── Airtable PAT (AECI-83) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by the Airtable gateway lib (apps/api/scripts/lib/airtable.ts) for the
# one-time bulk-migration tooling. Workers never read these. (The original
# Airtable → Supabase-Postgres bulk-migrate script is retired — the live curator
# → app-DB path is POST /api/promote into D1; see docs/API_CONTRACTS.md.)
#
# AIRTABLE_PAT: a Personal Access Token with scopes data.records:read,
# data.records:write, and schema.bases:write on the base below (the script
# creates a `supabase_uuid` field and writes the rec-ID→UUID mapping back).
AIRTABLE_PAT=
# The Airtable base holding the curator workspace.
AIRTABLE_BASE_ID=appy81IdGJY6Fngf9

# ─── Review-app promotion push (POST /api/promote) ─────────────────────────
# Bearer token the review application presents to push promoted records into
# Supabase. The WORKER reads this at runtime (unlike the migration vars above),
# so set it as a Wrangler secret in deployed envs:
#   wrangler secret put REVIEW_APP_TOKEN --env preview|staging|production
# Generate a high-entropy value, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Absent → every
# /api/promote request is rejected 401 (fail-closed).
REVIEW_APP_TOKEN=

# ─── Linear webhook signing (AECI-212 / Phase 6.5) ─────────────────────────
# HMAC-SHA256 signing secret for the inbound Linear webhook (POST /api/webhooks/
# linear). Copy it from the webhook's settings in Linear (Settings > API >
# Webhooks). The WORKER reads it at runtime, so set it as a Wrangler secret in
# deployed envs:
#   wrangler secret put LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET --env preview|staging|production
# Absent → every webhook is rejected 401 (fail-closed). For local testing,
# generate any value and sign requests with it:
#   printf '%s' "$BODY" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac "$SECRET"   # → Linear-Signature
LINEAR_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ─── Cache-tag purge after promote (AECI-105 / ADR 0010) ───────────────────
# The promote handler purges the affected edge cache tags by calling Cloudflare's
# purge-by-tag API DIRECTLY (no web↔api service binding — see ADR 0010). The
# WORKER reads both at runtime, so set them as Wrangler secrets/vars in deployed
# envs (staging + production):
#   wrangler secret put CF_PURGE_API_TOKEN --env staging|production
#   wrangler secret put CF_ZONE_ID         --env staging|production   # or a wrangler var
# CF_PURGE_API_TOKEN MUST be scoped to `Zone.Cache Purge` on aecintegrations.com
# only (docs/CACHE_STRATEGY.md §5) — same minimal scope as the web Worker's token.
# Absent (local `pnpm dev:bound`, PR previews) → promote skips the purge as a
# graceful no-op; pages fall back to the TTL (≤15 min).
CF_PURGE_API_TOKEN=
CF_ZONE_ID=

# ─── Datadog (AECI-31) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DD_API_KEY is the only required secret for `logToDatadog()` (Datadog Logs
# HTTP intake). When empty, the helper is a no-op so dev boots cleanly.
DD_API_KEY=
# Optional. Datadog region host. Defaults to datadoghq.com when unset.
# Examples: datadoghq.eu, us3.datadoghq.com, us5.datadoghq.com, ap1.datadoghq.com
DD_SITE=datadoghq.com

# ─── Algolia (AECI-134) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional until the sync pipeline lands (3.5/3.6) — the Worker reads neither at
# runtime yet, so leave empty for local dev. ALGOLIA_ADMIN_KEY is the per-env
# MANAGEMENT key (search + index-mutation ACLs, scoped to this env's indexes),
# NOT the app-wide root admin key. Provision real per-env values with
# `node scripts/algolia/provision.mjs` and push them with
# `wrangler secret put ALGOLIA_APP_ID/ALGOLIA_ADMIN_KEY --env <env>`.
ALGOLIA_APP_ID=
ALGOLIA_ADMIN_KEY=

# ─── Anthropic API toxicity scoring (AECI-258) ─────────────────────────────
# Anthropic API key. The WORKER reads it at runtime to score review bodies via
# Claude Haiku on POST /api/reviews, so set it as a Wrangler secret in deployed
# envs:
#   wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY --env staging|production
# Optional and FAIL-OPEN: absent (local dev, PR previews) → scoring is a silent
# no-op storing toxicity_score=null; an outage also stores null (logged warn).
# The score only flags the moderation queue — it never blocks a submission.
# Get one from https://console.anthropic.com (Settings → API Keys). Supersedes
# the sunsetting Google Perspective API (AECI-198).
# GDPR: the Messages API has no per-request no-store flag (unlike Perspective's
# doNotStore), so the Anthropic org behind a DEPLOYED key MUST have zero data
# retention (ZDR) enabled, or scored review bodies are retained ~30 days outside
# the §8 erasure boundary. (Local dev sends nothing unless you set a real key.)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ─── Resend transactional email (AECI-240 / Phase 7.5, §11.1) ───────────────
# RESEND_API_KEY is read at runtime by lib/email.ts for the review confirmation /
# approved / rejected emails, the account-deletion confirmation, and the
# reconcile-sweep admin alert. Set it as a Wrangler secret in deployed envs:
#   wrangler secret put RESEND_API_KEY --env staging|production
# Optional and FAIL-OPEN: absent (local dev, PR previews) → every send is a silent
# 'skipped' and the triggering action still succeeds. Get a key from
# https://resend.com (API Keys). The repo uses Resend, not the spec's original
# "Loops" — see docs/email.md. To exercise real sends locally, set a key AND
# EMAIL_FROM to a verified-domain sender below.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Sender for transactional email — the Resend `from`. Bare address or `Name <addr>`.
# Must be on a Resend-verified domain. Absent → sends skip (with RESEND_API_KEY).
EMAIL_FROM=
# Optional. Recipient of the reconcile-sweep stuck-request admin alert (§6.2).
ADMIN_ALERT_EMAIL=

# ─── IndexNow notification after promote (AECI-236 / §20.2) ─────────────────
# On promote, the WORKER submits the affected public URLs to IndexNow (Bing /
# Yandex / …). Two values, both read at runtime:
#   wrangler secret put INDEXNOW_KEY --env production   # 8–128 chars [A-Za-z0-9-]
#   PUBLIC_SITE_URL  → a wrangler var (apps/api/wrangler.jsonc), not a secret
# INDEXNOW_KEY must MATCH the web Worker's INDEXNOW_KEY (the SSR Worker serves the
# `{INDEXNOW_KEY}.txt` verification file). FAIL-OPEN: absent (local dev, PR
# previews, pre-launch) → the submission is a graceful no-op.
# PROVISION ONLY AT LAUNCH, on the env whose web Worker has ALLOW_INDEXING="true":
# pinging IndexNow for a noindex'd site is a correctness bug, so the key's absence
# is the enforcement. Generate a key with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 16`.
INDEXNOW_KEY=

# Public site base URL (no trailing slash) — SHARED by transactional email (the
# absolute links in the approved/rejected emails, AECI-240) AND the IndexNow
# submission (the origin the affected URLs are built against, AECI-236). Local
# default below; set the real launch host as a wrangler var in production. Absent →
# email links are omitted and IndexNow no-ops.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:8788
